# Give the head a stable MAC the moment the interface appears.
#
# ⚠️ /lib/udev/rules.d AND NOT /etc/udev/rules.d. The conventional place for a
# local rule is /etc, and it does not work here: this is buildroot's udev 220
# (eudev), and it reads rules from /lib/udev/rules.d ONLY. Verified on hardware
# 2026-08-27 -- `udevadm test /sys/class/net/eth0` listed every rules file it
# read and /etc/udev/rules.d appeared zero times. A rule placed in /etc is
# silently never loaded, which looks exactly like a rule that does not match.
# Do not "tidy" this back into /etc.
#
# udev and not an init script: eth0 arrives through the stmmac deferred probe,
# measured at t+73.9 s on a first boot -- well after S40network ran. Ordering
# by S-number cannot catch an interface that does not exist yet.
#
# See /usr/sbin/duco-macaddr for why U-Boot cannot do this itself.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="net", KERNEL=="eth*", RUN+="/usr/sbin/duco-macaddr %k"
